      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a quick comparison of ETFs and mutual funds for your memo.  Generally, ETFs are traded like stocks on an exchange, offering real-time liquidity, whereas mutual funds are priced once per day after the market closes. Management styles can vary, but many ETFs are passively managed to track an index, while mutual funds can be actively managed, aiming to beat the market.\n\n| Feature | ETFs (Exchange-Traded Funds) | Mutual Funds |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Liquidity** | High; traded throughout the day on exchanges. | Lower; priced and traded only once daily (after-hours). |\n| **Management Style** | Often passively managed (index tracking). | Can be actively or passively managed. |\n\nI hope this helps you draft your memo! Let me know if you need more details.",
